Package: snmpexporter
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: dhtech <dhtech@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= @PYTHON@~), python3 (<< @PYTHON_NEXT@), python3-twisted, python3-yaml, python3-objgraph, @LIBSNMP@, libc6 (>= @GLIBC@), passwd
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/dhtech/snmpexporter
Description: SNMP exporter for Prometheus that reads MIBs (snmpexporterd)
 snmpexporterd polls a device over SNMP when Prometheus asks it to
 (/probe?target=<device>&layer=<layer>) and answers with the device's
 values as metrics, named from the MIBs and labelled by joining tables
 (an interface counter carries the interface's name and description).
 snmpexport does one such poll from the command line.
 .
 The package holds the program, its compiled MIB resolver and the
 Net-SNMP Python module it polls with, built from
 github.com/dhtech/python3-netsnmp:
 @NETSNMP@.
 It holds no MIB files: where they are is said in
 /etc/default/snmpexporter (MIBDIRS, MIBS).
 .
 The unit snmpexporterd@<port>.service is installed; a first
 installation neither enables nor starts an instance.
